{"decision":"edit","issues":[{"quote":"all set against a uniform gray background.","problem":"The backdrop is not uniformly gray; a soft light area is visible near the lower edge and changes position relative to the holder."},{"quote":"The whole holder also drifts toward the right side of the frame","problem":"The holder does not show a clear continuous rightward drift; its position shifts back and forth within the frame."},{"quote":"The gray background remains unchanged throughout.","problem":"The background is not unchanged; the soft light area near the lower edge moves/appears in different positions, and the wording is too absolute."}],"caption":"The video showcases a pear-shaped blue gemstone gripped by four slender, curved metal prongs mounted on a short ridged cylindrical holder, all set against a mostly gray background. The assembly is already turning when the view opens, rotating slowly and steadily about a roughly vertical axis so that the prongs and the gem's pointed outline shift position relative to the camera within the frame.

Bright green and cyan sparkles appear, move, and fade across the facets as the stone changes angle, tracking the rotation rather than marking separate objects. The holder also shifts slightly within the frame, and the cylindrical base becomes more edge-on at times, showing more of its ridged wall and less of its open top. These continual shifts make the prongs move steadily around the gem, one curved prong crossing the front and another rising behind the stone.

The gray background stays mostly flat, with a soft light area near the lower edge. It gives a simple backdrop for the turning gem and moving metal prongs.","length_note":""}
